00:18:19.980 --> 00:18:22.580
Stop being such a tease and let me eat it!

00:18:22.580 --> 00:18:27.040
Don't tell me you're doing this on purpose!

00:18:22.580 --> 00:18:27.040
No, no, no, no~ You're so cold...

00:18:38.680 --> 00:18:41.800
Huh? I get the feeling that...

00:18:47.890 --> 00:18:50.980
Really now, what the heck am I doing?

00:18:51.310 --> 00:18:54.320
I was so stupid to get 
all worked up on my own.

00:18:54.320 --> 00:18:56.740
To Yuuji

00:18:55.190 --> 00:18:56.740
What is love? {baby don't hurt, no more}

00:18:57.400 --> 00:19:00.110
Hey! Are you there, Kazuki?

00:19:00.700 --> 00:19:02.490
Kazuki, I know you're in there!

00:19:02.490 --> 00:19:03.660
No I'm not!

00:19:04.120 --> 00:19:07.870
You know, we used to play here on this veranda..

00:19:07.410 --> 00:19:08.460
I guess we did.

00:19:09.080 --> 00:19:11.210
But it seems so small now.

00:19:12.130 --> 00:19:16.170
Also, it feels like the gap between
 the verandas used to be bigger.

00:19:16.170 --> 00:19:20.630
Of course it's going to look smaller as you get bigger.

00:19:21.430 --> 00:19:24.050
<i>What is it? What's he getting at?</i>

00:19:24.050 --> 00:19:27.270
<i>Is he trying to say that people change as they grow up?</i>

00:19:27.270 --> 00:19:29.350
<i>I can see the logic in that... {Ryoumi: If that's it, I would know that at any age. // imo this was a mishear of "ikutsu" instead of "rikutsu" ~Zalis}</i>

00:19:29.350 --> 00:19:31.810
<i>But somehow, I can't accept it.</i>

00:19:31.810 --> 00:19:35.860
<i>After all, I really loved Yuuji.</i>

00:19:35.860 --> 00:19:39.030
<i>In these ten years, the Yuuji I remembered...</i>

00:19:39.570 --> 00:19:42.780
...has become a world-class pervert!

00:19:43.660 --> 00:19:44.820
You know...

00:19:45.330 --> 00:19:48.950
...the first time we met was on this veranda.

00:19:50.370 --> 00:19:53.540
<i>Yuuji... remembered.</i>

00:19:58.380 --> 00:20:01.050
Hey, Yuuji, may I ask you a question?

00:20:01.050 --> 00:20:01.760
Sure.

00:20:02.260 --> 00:20:05.470
What did you think of me when we first met?

00:20:05.470 --> 00:20:10.020
Oh, I thought you were a really cute girl.

00:20:11.020 --> 00:20:12.310
Why'd you ask?

00:20:12.310 --> 00:20:15.020
I see...

00:20:22.780 --> 00:20:24.740
I guess I have no choice.

00:20:24.740 --> 00:20:27.990
It'd be a waste to throw this out 
after all I went through to bake it.

00:20:27.990 --> 00:20:29.450
So you can have so-

00:20:30.870 --> 00:20:32.960
Like he said, you're such a cute girl.

00:20:36.630 --> 00:20:38.920
What a nostalgic place this is.

00:20:38.920 --> 00:20:42.630
I remember playing some 
great games of house here.

00:20:43.470 --> 00:20:44.630
Yeah.

00:20:50.560 --> 00:20:53.520
How about a toast to our reunion?

00:20:53.520 --> 00:20:55.310
CHEERS!

00:20:55.310 --> 00:20:56.650
Yuuji & Marie-chan

00:20:55.310 --> 00:20:56.650
Welcome back!

00:20:56.980 --> 00:20:59.730
Aren't you glad you get to eat it?

00:20:59.730 --> 00:21:01.190
I guess so.

00:21:01.530 --> 00:21:04.360
It makes it worth staying up all night baking.

00:21:04.900 --> 00:21:05.660
Here.

00:21:05.660 --> 00:21:06.700
Thanks.

00:21:07.370 --> 00:21:09.080
Here I go.

00:21:18.750 --> 00:21:20.630
What is this?!

00:21:20.630 --> 00:21:23.300
Is this even fit for human consumption?

00:21:23.670 --> 00:21:25.260
I knew it.

00:21:25.260 --> 00:21:28.340
Kazuki-chan's cooking sense is a bit... senseless.

00:21:28.340 --> 00:21:32.310
Say what?! I really thought it would taste good.

00:21:32.310 --> 00:21:36.810
K-Kazuki, it's incredible. 
Incredibly awful, that is!

00:21:37.150 --> 00:21:39.810
And just <i>where</i> do you think you're touching me?!

00:21:39.810 --> 00:21:41.440
You pervert!

00:21:40.610 --> 00:21:42.360
Eliminating the threat.

00:21:41.440 --> 00:21:44.570
NOOO!!

00:21:46.450 --> 00:21:50.450
<i>And that's how our lives as neighbors
 began once again.</i>

00:21:51.370 --> 00:21:56.080
<i>Here at this veranda where
 Yuuji and I met for the first time.</i>

00:22:06.260 --> 00:22:14.890
The first time we met was on that sunlit veranda... {fi, link}

00:22:06.260 --> 00:22:14.890
Hajimete deatta hidamari no BERANDA

00:22:14.890 --> 00:22:20.520
Do you remember that place? {video fi, fo}

00:22:14.890 --> 00:22:20.520
Oboeteru kono basho?

00:22:21.900 --> 00:22:31.740
Spending time together was like breathing air, {sc, sc}

00:22:21.900 --> 00:22:31.740
Maru de kuuki no you na futari no jikan

00:22:31.740 --> 00:22:38.540
and we didn't realize the beauty of that placid time. {fo? or sc}

00:22:31.740 --> 00:22:38.540
SUTEKI na koto kizukanai PLACID TIME

00:22:39.080 --> 00:22:46.050
Our feelings of missing each other gave birth to... {sc, link}

00:22:39.080 --> 00:22:46.050
Aitai kimochi kara umareta

00:22:46.050 --> 00:22:50.680
...the dreams that bloomed in our hearts, {link, link}

00:22:46.050 --> 00:22:50.680
Kokoro ni saku yume wo

00:22:50.680 --> 00:22:56.310
which became more and more colorful. {link, link}

00:22:50.680 --> 00:22:56.310
Nan domo irozuiteku dakara

00:22:56.310 --> 00:23:03.520
Will you let me stay by your side? {link, link}

00:22:56.310 --> 00:23:03.520
Anata no tonari ni isasete ne

00:23:03.520 --> 00:23:07.900
I hope our silhouettes... {link, link}

00:23:03.520 --> 00:23:07.900
Futatsu no SHIRUETTO

00:23:07.900 --> 00:23:19.790
...will continue this endless story tomorrow. {link, fo}

00:23:07.900 --> 00:23:19.790
Ashita mo tsuzuku to ii na endless story

